# Map, GPS, routing and checkpoint constraints
- Consult `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `PROJECT_SPEC.md` sections 7-9.
- A map library is not a place database or route provider. Evaluate MapLibre + legitimate basemap/provider versus Google Maps before permanent SDK lock-in. Follow provider attribution and licensing requirements; do not mix restricted provider data into an incompatible map.
- Real GPS is opt-in; use the browser Geolocation API only in a secure context, report denied/unavailable/low-accuracy states, and stop `watchPosition` on cleanup. Never imply reliable background tracking.
- When outside the Kyoto demo area, don't teleport the real fox into Kyoto. Offer an explicit switch to **Kyoto Demo Mode**.
- Keep demo position/movement and real GPS state separate. Label sample congestion, simulated check-ins and fictional rewards.
- Curated walk routes must align with actual public walking paths, avoiding straight-line shortcuts through waterways, buildings, or private property.
- Grant each checkpoint/mission reward only once per completion instance; handle repeated GPS callbacks and rerenders idempotently.
- Keep resident sensitivity in mind: do not route tourists into quiet residential areas merely to move crowds.
